course: dictionary
lesson: 14375
title: Ordinal numbers: first, second, third
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Numbers do two different jobs. Cardinal numbers tell you how many things there are: 1, 2, 3. Ordinal numbers tell you the place or position of something in an order: first, second, third, and so on.
explain: «Mia came second in the race.» Second is an ordinal number. It tells you Mia's place, not how many runners there were. Ordinal numbers in digits end in st, nd, rd or th: 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th, 21st.
explain: Ordinal numbers are everywhere: «Our class is on the third floor.» «Sam is at the front of the queue, in first position.» Ask yourself: is this number telling me how many, or which place in the order? If it tells you which place, it is ordinal.
fact: An ordinal number shows position or place in an order.
fact: «First», «second» and «third» are ordinal numbers, and so are «4th» and «21st».
fact: «Cardinal» numbers, such as 1, 2 and 3, tell you how many things there are.
fact: An ordinal number answers the question "which one?", while a cardinal number answers "how many?"
fact: In digits, ordinal numbers end in st, nd, rd or th, such as 1st, 2nd, 3rd and 4th.
exercise: «Ella finished the race in third place.» What kind of number is third here? | *Ordinal, it shows the place in the order | Fraction, it shows a part of a whole | Decimal, it shows a point | Cardinal, it counts how many
exercise: «There are 5 apples in the bowl.» What kind of number is 5 here? | Ordinal, it shows the first apple | Ordinal, it shows the place in the order | *Cardinal, it counts how many | Percentage, it shows a share
exercise: Which ordinal number comes straight after third? | *Fourth | Fifth | First | Second
test:  «Lily is 5th in the line for lunch.» What does 5th show? | *Her place in the line | The number of children in the line | The cost of her lunch | The time lunch starts
test: Which word is an ordinal number? | Eighty | Eight apples | *Eighth | Eight
exam: «The shop is on the 4th floor.» What does 4th show? | The number of floors in the shop | *Its position in the order of floors | The name of the shop | The price of the shop
